{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772651018,"nonce":"CLhSH06IDqfnXwaY25NdFWBA9oY=","title":"auth-merge auto-fix deletes user content from untracked directories","message":"## Severity: Critical — data-loss bug\n\nWhen the main worktree has an untracked directory that contains a file tracked on the feature branch, auth-merges auto-fix logic deletes the ENTIRE directory, permanently removing user content unrelated to the merge.\n\n**Incident (2026-03-03):** Merging a feature branch that added `20 Writing/15 Series/probability-theory/_series.md` triggered auto-fix on the `probability-theory/` directory. The directory contained user writing files (`channels.mdx`, `events.mdx`, `functions.mdx`, `assets/`, `diagrams/`) that were untracked in the main worktree. All were deleted using `rm -rf`, bypassing macOS Trash. Content was recovered from Time Machine (Feb 24 backup).\n\n**Root cause:** The auto-fix correctly identifies that an untracked directory contains a file that will be introduced by the merge (creating a conflict). But it removes the ENTIRE directory, not just the conflicting file.\n\n**Correct fix:** Only remove the specific file path that conflicts with the incoming tracked file, not the entire parent directory. Or: stash/move the directory, let the merge add the tracked file, then restore the rest.\n\n**Status:** Fixed in dotfiles retro-fixes branch. This issue tracks the fix landing in the standalone repo.\n\nMigrated from dotfiles issue 353974d.","files":null}]}